At the time this licensing notice was adopted, the repository was primarily documentation-first; the Apache-2.0 scope is intended to govern software code added under this repository policy unless explicitly stated otherwise.

3. Third-party material

Third-party material remains subject to its original license, copyright, attribution, or other applicable terms. A more specific notice attached to a file or imported work overrides this repository-level default for that material.

4. Names, marks, and endorsement

These licenses do not grant a right to claim that a modified work, fork, product, or service is an official AranSoul release or is endorsed by the AranSoul Project. Rights in names, logos, marks, and source-identifying designations are separate from the copyright permissions granted above, except to the extent use is legally permitted for attribution, identification, or other applicable purposes.

5. Scope clarity

Public availability, participation in the repository, or the presence of a historical artifact does not change the governance status of that material. Licensing permission to copy or adapt content is separate from whether a concept is CURRENT, CANDIDATE, HISTORICAL, or RETIRED / UNVERIFIED within AranSoul's own project governance.
